    "title": "Former federal corrections officer sentenced to 12 years for child sex abuse - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Becca Yanez No media credit provided. ,\n9 hours ago\nPORTLAND, Ore. ( KOIN ) – A former federal corrections officer from Sheridan was sentenced to 12 years for child sexual abuse on Tuesday, the Polk County District Attorney’s office announced Wednesday.\nPeter Nicholas Fles, Jr., 41, pleaded no contest to two counts of first-degree sex abuse by abusing a child under the age of 14 in West Salem.\nClose Thanks for signing up!\nWatch for us in your inbox.\nSubscribe Now\nEye on Northwest Politics A Polk County judge sentenced him to 12 years and five months in prison plus nearly four years of post-release supervision. Fles is also required to register as a sex offender and will not be eligible for early release.\nCopyright 2026 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to KOIN.com.\n3",
    "summary": ", PORTLAND, Ore. ( KOIN ) – A former federal corrections officer from Sheridan was sentenced to 12 years for child sexual abuse on Tuesday, the Polk County District Attorney’s office announced Wednesday. Peter Nicholas Fles, Jr., 41, pleaded no contest to two counts of first-degree sex abuse by abusing a child under the age of 14 in West Salem. Eye on Northwest Politics A Polk County judge sentenced him to 12 years and five months in prison plus nearly four years of post-release supervision.",
